# The zipline rope needs its own render types: the rope emits POSITION_COLOR_LIGHTMAP in QUADS and
# has a culled and an unculled variant (the Enable3DRenderingForZipline config switch), which no
# vanilla pipeline matches.
#
# 1.21.5 deleted RenderStateShard's shader and cull shards (RenderStateShard$CullStateShard and
# RENDERTYPE_LEASH_SHADER are gone from the class) and moved the vertex format, the primitive mode
# and culling into the RenderPipeline, so the composite state is now built around a pipeline:
#   - RenderType.create(String, int, RenderPipeline, CompositeState) is package-private,
#   - CompositeState$CompositeStateBuilder's setters and createCompositeState are protected,
#   - the two state shards ParCool still uses (NO_TEXTURE, LIGHTMAP) are protected,
#   - RenderPipelines#MATRICES_COLOR_FOG_SNIPPET - the snippet RenderPipelines.LEASH itself is built
#     from - is private, and a pipeline whose declared uniform set does not match what
#     core/rendertype_leash reads fails to compile at first draw,
#   - RenderPipelines#PIPELINES_BY_LOCATION is private, and it is the map the game precompiles
#     ShaderManager's pipelines from at every resource reload.
# The NeoForge side gets the same members through
# neoforge/src/main/resources/META-INF/accesstransformer.cfg.
